# Milestone: M3
# Covers: raising a new exception inside a finally/onleave body (C-1
#         replace-on-raise): the new exception wins; the original unwind is
#         silently suppressed.
#
# deferred: v1.x — onleave clause not implemented (PARSE-033 open; deferred-v1.x per matrix)
# matrix-row: tag-onleave
#
# Reason: the C-level replace-on-raise (C-1) mechanism is fully implemented
# in run_cleanup_with_replace() at M3 and is covered by the integration test
# tests/chk/control_transfer/throw_in_finally.chk.  However, the
# corresponding tag-stop-inside-finally variant (where a tag.stop() inside a
# finally body replaces an in-progress throw) requires UTag runtime (T29) and
# is not testable in urbiscript until then.  Additionally, testing force-stop
# from a host callback during finally requires T30 (OP_PUSH_TAG runtime
# extension for cross-strand force).
#
# When T29/T30 land, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: throw is suppressed by tag.stop() in finally body;
# the tag stop wins.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29/T30):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var side = 0;
#   t: {
#     try {
#       throw 42
#     } finally {
#       side = 1;
#       t.stop()
#     }
#   };
#   side
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 1
